7707	{"artifactId":"LLD-83c85f38afad7843-s1","entry":{"id":"review-90752b2701f0fdeb941afeeb78dc2b61","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:45:00.842Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Request-correlated completion addresses the ISSUE's premature first-result termination in both readers.","evidence":"The ISSUE describes an earlier empty result hiding the real reply. Claude mapLine currently maps every result to done; run calls 'void drain(stdout)' and returns, while resume returns on done/error. The retained probe's result contains the submitted UUID in both user_message_uuid and user_message_uuids. The proposed matching rule directly addresses these paths; Codex protocol verification remains an explicit implementation requirement. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-83c85f38afad7843.json, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, /tmp/insrc-issue83-wire-probe/probe.py, /tmp/insrc-issue83-wire-probe/summary.json]","action":"Implement both reader paths and retain the planned Codex protocol verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The relationship documentation and sequence companion adequately describe the proposed interaction.","evidence":"Section 3 documents host-turn ownership, UUID-to-frame cardinality and legacy compatibility. The linked HTML exists, and its Mermaid source depicts UUID submission, ignoring earlier results, forwarding content and checkpointing completion. Rendering could not be verified: headless Chrome failed with 'Failed to create a unique user data directory for headless' in this restricted environment. [files: docs/standalone/keep-chat-turn-s-reply-when-E2026101383c85f38/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the existing companion in a writable browser environment and verify its consistency before signoff.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Claude currently uses a positional prompt, completes on its first result, and omits terminal-line progress checkpoints.","evidence":"buildArgs appends 'args.push('--', req.prompt)'. The result branch returns done without correlation checks. Both reader loops return on terminal events before their onProgress call. Existing tests explicitly assert 'a position after each line before the terminal one' and 'a position after the non-terminal line'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts]","action":"Update these behaviors and the corresponding existing assertions together.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The adapter can own UUID framing/classification while existing output and lifecycle consumers carry the opaque turnId without a schema migration.","evidence":"ProviderMapper, TurnState, run, resume and nodeSpawner are in cli-adapter.ts. SegmentCursor already stores a string turnId; session-output creates markers and advances cursors with that identity. turn-lifecycle copies turnId into liveTurn and matches identities by equality. Production stdin is already piped for Claude and exposes write(). The identified adapter/output boundaries support the proposed change. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fixtures.ts]","action":"Keep framing provider-specific and update adapter fixtures/tests alongside the implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Legacy replay preserves the latest native result outcome across repeated reloads while checkpointing ignored results.","evidence":"resume initializes 'const state: TurnState = {}' and reads only from req.cursor. SegmentCursor contains only sessionId, turnId, generation and offset. The proposed legacy reader checkpoints a result and retains its outcome only in reader state. If the window reloads after the last result but before process exit, the next reader starts after that result and cannot recover its outcome; at EOF it falsely reports no result. The design specifies reconstruction of UUID identity, but no reconstruction of legacy result state. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"Specify how legacy resume reconstructs the latest result before the saved offset, or durably retains that outcome. Add a two-reload regression: checkpoint a failed legacy result, reload before exit, then verify its native failure message survives EOF.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Prompt completion can remain independent of process exit without releasing the session lease or disabling process controls.","evidence":"run keeps the live process entry until proc.exit and marks terminal before yielding, avoiding cleanup kills. turn-lifecycle attaches the lease to the process exit rather than reader completion. Existing hanging-process tests assert no kill after done and verify stop resolves after exit. resume guards process signaling with liveness/start-time checks. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts]","action":"Preserve these mechanisms when changing completion classification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping supplies executable regression scenarios for reply retention, prompt completion, durable identity and provider separation.","evidence":"The existing fake spawner records stdin writes and supports hangUntilKilled; adapter tests already exercise file-backed output, saved-offset resume and process controls. These seams support the proposed dynamic-UUID early-result regressions and terminal checkpoint assertions, which fail against the current unconditional result completion. Codex item/turn tests provide compatibility coverage rather than a Claude-defect regression. These are planned tests, not verified passing implementations. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fixtures.ts, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-83c85f38afad7843-s1.json]","action":"Add the legacy repeated-reload case identified above, implement the mapped regressions, and record failing-before/passing-after evidence. Re-establish the baseline: the current test file contains duplicate readFileSync and tick imports, so the historical 88/88 statement is not current validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T16:45:00.842Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
