6389	{"artifactId":"LLD-83c85f38afad7843-s1","entry":{"id":"review-43b5cf5a8d4bf6bf1f2fd2df66b9713c","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:52:16.286Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Request-correlated completion in both readers addresses the ISSUE's premature completion root cause.","evidence":"The ISSUE states that an earlier queued result hides the user's reply. Claude mapLine currently maps every result to done; run drains subsequent output and resume returns immediately. The retained probe records the submitted UUID in both result correlation fields. The design changes both readers, includes legacy recovery, and explicitly requires independent Codex protocol verification. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-83c85f38afad7843.json, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, docs/standalone/keep-chat-turn-s-reply-when-E2026101383c85f38/S001/claude-correlation-probe.json]","action":"Implement the specified correlation and serial protocol checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Claude currently uses positional prompts and both readers finish at the first terminal result.","evidence":"buildArgs appends '--', req.prompt. Claude result handling returns done unconditionally. run invokes 'void drain(stdout)' before returning on terminal events; resume yields the terminal event and returns. Both place onProgress after that return, so terminal lines currently bypass checkpointing. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"Replace first-result completion and checkpoint the accepted terminal before yielding it, as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The adapter and session-output implementation provide the required production change sites without a cursor schema migration.","evidence":"ProviderMapper, TurnState, run, resume and nodeSpawner are in cli-adapter.ts. SessionOutput.tail, fileFor and turnStartOffset are in session-output.ts. turn-lifecycle copies turnId, generation and offset into saved liveTurn state without parsing provider identity. Existing tail options can be extended additively. Analyzer coverage was incomplete, so these conclusions also use direct source reads and turnId consumer searches. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"Include nodeSpawner's swallowed write failures in implementation review, and update adapter/session-output tests alongside production changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Prompt completion can remain separate from process lifetime, lease ownership, cancellation and opaque cursor identity.","evidence":"run retains its live process entry until proc.exit and avoids killing after a terminal event. turn-lifecycle attaches the lease to the process and explicitly releases it on process exit rather than answer completion. resume guards signaling with PID/start-time checks. The existing hangUntilKilled test asserts reader completion while the process remains alive and receives no kill signal. The proposed correlation changes fit these boundaries. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts]","action":"Keep these lifecycle paths intact and run the specified stop, lease, PID-reuse and alive-after-result regressions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked sequence companion renders consistently with the proposed interaction.","evidence":"Inspected the generated HTML and embedded Mermaid source. It describes UUID input, ignoring an earlier result, forwarding content, checkpointing the own terminal and leaving the process alive. The prose separately documents request/frame ownership and legacy compatibility adequately. No rendered browser inspection was performed, so layout and successful Mermaid rendering are unverified. [files: docs/standalone/keep-chat-turn-s-reply-when-E2026101383c85f38/S001/sequence-diagram.html]","action":"Render the supplied companion and inspect it before claiming visual verification; correct or regenerate it if rendering fails.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping supplies discriminating tests for all four criteria.","evidence":"ac1 specifies earlier results followed by user content in pipe/file modes; current code would truncate that content. ac2 uses an alive process and own UUID result; current code would finish on the earlier result. ac3 covers midstream identity, terminal checkpoints and repeated legacy reload preserving failure; current resume neither reconstructs earlier outcomes nor checkpoints terminal lines. ac4 protects existing Codex item/turn separation and adds protocol evidence. Existing tests demonstrate fake-process, temporary output, saved-offset and liveness seams needed for these cases. This verifies the test design, not implementation or a passing baseline. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/cli-adapter.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-output.ts]","action":"Add and demonstrate failing regressions before implementation, then execute the proposed affected suites and TypeScript checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T16:52:16.286Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
